# `std/io/msg/nats_jetstream`

```hql
module io.msg.nats_jetstream
```

NATS JetStream: one subject of a stream, as a transport read by `tap`
and written by `sink` and `target` like any other endpoint (module
`io`). A stream keeps what is published to its subjects, so a read
starts where it says, and a message is written once the stream
acknowledges it. The `nats_jetstream` kind of a configured endpoint is
this transport under an id. A program imports the module:
`import io.msg.nats_jetstream`.

- [`NatsJetStream`](types/NatsJetStream.hmd) — One subject of a JetStream stream on a NATS server.
- [`nats_jetstream`](nats_jetstream.hmd) — The subject `subject` of the stream `stream`, as a `NatsJetStream` transport; its parameters are the keys of the `nats_jetstream` kind.
<!-- hql reference: end -->
